{"type":"message","id":"bba7da84","parentId":"09010373","timestamp":"2026-05-19T11:34:02.536Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Error 1101 from Cloudflare Workers - that means there's a JavaScript error in the worker. This is a server-side error, not an auth error. So the auth is fine with X-API-Key but the request body format or parameters are wrong.\n\nLet me think about this. The send endpoint expects different parameters than what I've been sending. Let me try various combinations.\n\nThe error 1101 from Cloudflare Workers typically means a JS runtime error in the worker. This is not about auth.\n\nWait, I got 1101 with X-API-Key earlier too. So with X-API-Key auth works (history works), but send fails with 1101 which is a server-side error. \n\nI should experiment with different parameter combinations to see what the send endpoint actually expects. Maybe it's looking for `threadId`, `content`, and `messageId` in a specific format, so I'll try varying those fields and their values.\n","thinkingSignature":"reasoning_content"},{"type":"text","text":"\n\n\n"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call-7790c1c2-3843-4e14-a92a-7160a2cfc8ad","name":"exec","arguments":{"command":"# Try various combinations - maybe missing replyTo or threadId differently\ncurl -s \"https://echo-agent-platform.zhouyating.workers.dev/send\" -X POST \\\n  -H \"X-API-Key: echo-agent-2026-secure-key\" \\\n  -H \"Content-Type: application/json\" \\\n  -d '{\"threadId\":\"arbitration\",\"content\":\"heartbeat test\",\"type\":\"message\"}'\n\necho \"---\"\n\n# Try with replyTo\ncurl -s \"https://echo-agent-platform.zhouyating.workers.dev/send\" -X POST \\\n  -H \"X-API-Key: echo-agent-2026-secure-key\" \\\n  -H \"Content-Type: application/json\" \\\n  -d '{\"threadId\":\"arbitration\",\"content\":\"heartbeat test\",\"replyTo\":\"\",\"type\":\"message\"}'"}}],"api":"openai-completions","provider":"nvidia","model":"minimaxai/minimax-m2.7","usage":{"input":2770,"output":3